  "details": "This is a deeply empathetic idea with immense human value. Preserving and centralizing the memories of a loved one in a single place—where their friends can share photos, stories, and happy moments—transforms grief into a space of collaborative tribute and collective comfort.\n\n​📌 Concept Name\n\n​MEMORIAL ACCOUNT: MEMORY WALL\n\n​💡 Rationale and Purpose\n\n​When a friend or active community member passes away, their digital footprint often remains scattered across different platforms or private conversations. Creating this special status aims to provide a respectful space to:\n\n​Honor Their Memory: Unify shared photos, screenshots, and moments.\n\n​Support Community Grieving: Allow close friends to share anecdotes, reflect on happy times, and offer mutual comfort.\n\n​Preserve Their Legacy: Prevent the account from being lost to inactivity or having their contributions forgotten over time.\n\n​🛠️ Proposed Mechanics and Functionality\n\n​1. Respectful Verification\n\n​Support Request: Verified friends or family members submit a request through the official support channel.\n\n​Confirmation: The support/moderation team validates the information before transitioning the account state to prevent misuse.\n\n​2. Account and Interface Changes\n\n​Memorial Badge/Status: The account receives a subtle visual badge (such as the 🕊️ icon or a special tag) indicating that the profile is in memorial mode.\n\n​Read-Only Mode: Direct messages and active notifications are disabled to protect the original privacy of the profile.\n\n​3. The \"Memory & Story Wall\"\n\n​Collaborative Gallery: A special tab on the profile opens, allowing added friends to upload photographs taken with the deceased user.\n\n​Anecdote Section: A dedicated comment space exclusively for sharing positive stories, fun moments, and heartfelt words.\n\n​Community Moderation: Options for family or designated admins to keep the section respectful and free of inappropriate content.\n\n​\"Transforming the profile of someone who has passed into a living book of memories allows their light to keep shining for those who loved them.\"\n\n​En memoria de PauletteTheHoe.",
